{"name":"Remembrance","hex":"#ca9e9c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"remembrance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of remembering; a holding in mind, or bringing to mind; recollection.","The state of being remembered, or held in mind; memory, recollection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remember; to recall to mind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remembrance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Day of Remembrance for Truth and Justice","blocks":[{"text":"The Day of Remembrance for Truth and Justice is a public holiday in Argentina, commemorating the victims of the Civic-military dictatorship of Argentina. It is held on 24 March, the anniversary of the coup d'état of 1976 that brought the National Reorganization Process to power."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Bandera_de_los_Desaparecidos_-_D%C3%ADa_de_la_Memoria.jpg/330px-Bandera_de_los_Desaparecidos_-_D%C3%ADa_de_la_Memoria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day_of_Remembrance_for_Truth_and_Justice","wikidata":"Q2071460"},{"title":"Remembrance Day","blocks":[{"text":"Remembrance Day is a memorial day observed in former countries of the British Empire, and current Commonwealth member states since the end of the First World War to honour armed forces members who have died in the line of duty. The day is also marked by war remembrances in several other non-Commonwealth countries. In most countries, Remembrance Day is observed on 11 November to recall the end of First World War hostilities. Hostilities ended \"at the 11th hour of the 11th day of the 11th month\" of 1918, in accordance with the armistice signed by representatives of Germany and the Entente between 5:12 and 5:20 that morning. The First World War formally ended with the signing of the Treaty of Versailles on 28 June 1919."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Royal_British_Legion%27s_Paper_Poppy_-_white_background.jpg/330px-Royal_British_Legion%27s_Paper_Poppy_-_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remembrance_Day","wikidata":"Q27631"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg/500px-11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg/1280px-11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg/500px-11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Australian Minister of Defence, Stephen Smith, lays a wreath at the Eternal flame in Kings Park, Western Australia on Remembrance Day, 2011","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A11_Nov_gnangarra-15.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg/500px-Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg/1280px-Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg/500px-Sydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sydney Opera House shells were illuminated with poppies on Remembrance Day","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASydney_Opera_House_Remembrance_Day_2025-11-11.jpg"},{"srcset":"http